WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:06.601
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:08.316 --> 00:00:09.820
All right. I've figured it out.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.294
You guys are zombies.

00:00:11.294 --> 00:00:14.643
Not the horror movie kind, but
the honest-to-God voodoo kind.

00:00:14.643 --> 00:00:18.234
Somebody resurrected you from the dead
and he's on his lunch break or something

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:21.891
so that's why you're just standing here
next to all these lasers and guns.

00:00:21.891 --> 00:00:26.558
I can't help you guys because your brains
are being controlled by somebody else.

00:00:26.558 --> 00:00:28.727
Oh, yeah, see, there's your
master up there.

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:31.569
I should go talk to him. Maybe I
can buy one of you off him.

00:00:31.569 --> 00:00:33.525
You could help out around the
house or something.

00:00:33.525 --> 00:00:35.089
Besides, I have a gun.

00:00:35.089 --> 00:00:37.367
Everything's for sale when you have a gun.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:41.022
I know how to talk to these
people; I've been to Haiti.

00:00:41.022 --> 00:00:44.033
Les yeux de Dieu
ne regardent pas beaucoup là.

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:46.834
Hey, is that some more ammo?

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.400
All right! High-five!

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.729
Well... forget it.

00:00:51.729 --> 00:00:54.139
I am a little envious of those
guys, actually;

00:00:54.139 --> 00:00:56.509
just standing there next to
things that could kill them.

00:00:56.509 --> 00:00:58.005
I wish I could be like that.

00:00:58.005 --> 00:01:00.290
Just not care whether I live or die.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:04.178
Considering every retarded risk
I've taken this morning,

00:01:04.178 --> 00:01:06.388
you'd think I don't care, but I do.

00:01:06.388 --> 00:01:07.609
I don't want to die.

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:10.884
I want other people to die FOR me.

00:01:10.884 --> 00:01:13.247
SCIENTIST: Rescued at last!
Thank GOD you're here!

00:01:13.247 --> 00:01:14.615
Ah, the rescue team!

00:01:14.615 --> 00:01:15.927
[machine gun fire]

00:01:15.927 --> 00:01:18.342
Or, um... what?

00:01:18.342 --> 00:01:22.711
Okay, I can understand shooting
someone running at you screaming, but...

00:01:22.711 --> 00:01:25.426
I dunno, this feels shady.

00:01:25.426 --> 00:01:27.040
Is there another way out of here?

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.189
I think this guy's in a bad mood.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.695
No... all right, fine.

00:01:31.695 --> 00:01:33.501
I'll try and go make friends,

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.734
even though that always
ends up the same way.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:39.864
See, he's not even trying to
plant a gun on him or hide the body.

00:01:39.864 --> 00:01:44.133
That's a bad sign. Like this is
just another day at work for him.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.927
I'll at least give him some
warning so I don't sneak up on him.

00:01:46.927 --> 00:01:48.605
HECU: Maintain lookout.

00:01:48.605 --> 00:01:50.229
This guy's jumpy.

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:51.547
Hey, killer. What's up?

00:01:51.547 --> 00:01:52.347
[machine gun fire]

00:01:52.347 --> 00:01:53.872
[machine gun fire]
God! Jesus! Shit...

00:01:53.872 --> 00:01:54.605
Dammit.

00:01:54.605 --> 00:01:56.434
Diplomacy sucks!

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:58.033
[machine gun fire]
OW!

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.447
Man, what's your problem?!

00:02:01.447 --> 00:02:03.788
And why are you shooting everyone?!

00:02:03.788 --> 00:02:06.131
I'm taking this gun away
from you, mister.

00:02:06.131 --> 00:02:09.002
You're obviously not mature
enough to handle it.

00:02:09.002 --> 00:02:11.800
Now, you sit there and think
about what you've done.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.414
Somebody needs to explain what
the term "rescue" means to that guy.

00:02:15.414 --> 00:02:18.243
It does NOT mean whatever
he thinks it means.

00:02:18.243 --> 00:02:19.669
Well, more ammo.

00:02:19.669 --> 00:02:23.117
I wish I could save all this for
a rainy day, but the way this day's going,

00:02:23.117 --> 00:02:25.526
it must be pouring outside right now.

00:02:25.526 --> 00:02:29.506
Not that I'd know anything about that;
I'm still stuck in these catacombs.

00:02:29.506 --> 00:02:32.003
So, yeah, guess I just killed a guy.

00:02:32.003 --> 00:02:34.368
Totally on purpose this time.

00:02:34.368 --> 00:02:37.467
I'll just keep on moving and not
really think about that.

00:02:38.171 --> 00:02:40.235
SCIENTIST: Don't kill me! I'm
with the Science Team!

00:02:40.235 --> 00:02:44.406
Hey, me too, but you go on first
just in case they're not cool with that.

00:02:44.406 --> 00:02:45.913
[machine gun fire]

00:02:45.913 --> 00:02:48.864
Yeah, see, I'm just getting
some bad vibes here.

00:02:48.864 --> 00:02:50.912
Is there another floor I can get off on?

00:02:50.912 --> 00:02:52.959
I think this is the wrong one.

00:02:52.959 --> 00:02:54.144
No...

00:02:54.144 --> 00:02:55.639
Well, maybe I'm being a pessimist,

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:59.278
but I just don't think I'm going
to get along with these guys.

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:03.462
It's like a throwback to high school where
everyone had their--oh, more ammo--

00:03:03.462 --> 00:03:07.748
where everyone had their own cliques and you
had to watch what you said to which group.

00:03:07.748 --> 00:03:10.776
I guess the difference is here
there won't be so much drama.

00:03:10.776 --> 00:03:14.369
We all have guns so we should be
able to work out our differences pretty quickly,

00:03:14.369 --> 00:03:16.634
and won't have to draw this out
over the school year.

00:03:17.182 --> 00:03:18.133
CUT IT OUT!

00:03:19.907 --> 00:03:23.324
SEE, YOU GUYS PROBABLY NEVER GOT
OVER THIS CRAP FROM HIGH SCHOOL!

00:03:23.324 --> 00:03:24.801
I WENT ON TO COLLEGE!

00:03:25.103 --> 00:03:25.567
OW!

00:03:26.892 --> 00:03:29.462
I HAVE A DOCTOR'S DEGREE!

00:03:29.462 --> 00:03:30.834
You guys are dicks!

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:33.413
I know what's going on here.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:37.152
Every one of you wants to be the
big hero for rescuing us

00:03:37.152 --> 00:03:39.613
but you can't decide so you
fight over it.

00:03:39.613 --> 00:03:43.824
Instead of taking turns, you just shoot
anyone who walks out the door

00:03:43.824 --> 00:03:46.282
so that no one else can take
credit for the rescue.

00:03:46.282 --> 00:03:47.617
God damn!

00:03:47.617 --> 00:03:48.693
Congratulations!

00:03:48.693 --> 00:03:49.728
You won the prize!

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:51.133
You're all dead.

00:03:52.764 --> 00:03:53.467
Yuck...

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.362
So, how many people have I
killed now? Three or four?

00:03:57.362 --> 00:04:02.600
I think that one guy killed his buddy with
a grenade, which doesn't surprise me at all.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.267
Okay, left... right...

00:04:06.164 --> 00:04:08.793
I'll go this way, I'll just
crawl this time.

00:04:08.793 --> 00:04:09.926
Save my back.

00:04:09.926 --> 00:04:12.632
I still don't even know what
any of these lasers do,

00:04:12.632 --> 00:04:15.173
just that it's probably not good.

00:04:15.173 --> 00:04:19.048
I don't think these are like those
coupon dispensers at the grocery store.

00:04:19.048 --> 00:04:22.778
Man, I don't think I want to go
this way; I'm just going to turn around.

00:04:22.778 --> 00:04:25.137
So, yeah. I'm killing people now.

00:04:25.137 --> 00:04:29.527
But that was NOT murder. That
was TOTALLY self-defense.

00:04:29.527 --> 00:04:33.104
Just because I had a submachine
gun doesn't change anything.

00:04:33.104 --> 00:04:35.368
It just lets me defend more efficiently.

00:04:35.368 --> 00:04:37.499
I haven't murdered anyone.

00:04:37.499 --> 00:04:39.202
Err, not today, anyway.

00:04:39.202 --> 00:04:41.339
All right, where am I going?

00:04:41.339 --> 00:04:44.874
I think I did a U-turn again;
this looks like a dead end.

00:04:44.874 --> 00:04:47.029
There's no steps, of course.

00:04:47.029 --> 00:04:50.477
Well this conveyor might go
somewhere, but it's going the wrong way.

00:04:50.477 --> 00:04:52.200
Yeah, I don't wanna--WHOA!

00:04:53.573 --> 00:04:56.529
Okay, fuck this. There's gotta
be another way out of here.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.667
Oh, hey, I can just climb up there.

00:04:59.363 --> 00:04:59.801
Okay...

00:05:02.413 --> 00:05:04.588
HECU: No sign objective, sir.

00:05:04.588 --> 00:05:05.534
Oh no.

00:05:06.976 --> 00:05:08.888
So, we going to play nice, or...?

00:05:08.888 --> 00:05:10.534
HECU: Movement! Shit!
Nope.

00:05:12.269 --> 00:05:15.152
Well, looks like my armor's
better than yours.

00:05:15.152 --> 00:05:18.558
And I'll just loot your bodies
because that's how I roll.

00:05:18.558 --> 00:05:22.451
And that puts me at six or seven
counts of self defense.

00:05:22.451 --> 00:05:23.267
All right.

00:05:24.627 --> 00:05:28.300
Heeeeyyyyy!  "Surface Access"!

00:05:29.084 --> 00:05:29.968
Yes!

00:05:31.288 --> 00:05:32.234
Score!

00:05:33.563 --> 00:05:34.817
[exhale]

00:05:34.817 --> 00:05:39.716
Y'know, I think murder used to be
legal in Texas, if it was in your house

00:05:39.716 --> 00:05:42.367
and your wife was having sex
with another man.

00:05:42.858 --> 00:05:45.399
Hm, maybe you had to be drunk, too.

00:05:45.399 --> 00:05:48.300
They have drive-through
beer stands in Texas.

